id: core/holarchy
title: "Yawn holarchy and relations"
kind: ontology-contract
status: draft-0.2
updated: 2026-08-13

definition: >
  A Yawn is a durable whole that may also contribute as a part of a larger
  orientation contract. Containment uses one acyclic primary-parent backbone;
  non-containment meaning uses typed lateral relations.

primary_tree:
  maximum_primary_parents: 1
  cycles_allowed: false
  roots_allowed: true
  child_rule: >
    A child is independently inspectable and its proof, maintenance, inquiry,
    safety, or holding outcome advances or protects the parent contract.
  derived_index: child references are derived from primary-parent relations

lateral_relations:
  - overlaps
  - depends_on
  - supports
  - conflicts_with
  - coordinates_with
  - derived_from
  - supersedes
  - same_as

relation_requirements:
  - attributed-asserting-agent
  - source-or-evidence-refs
  - epistemic-status
  - confidence
  - lifecycle-status
  - effective-time

inheritance:
  authority: "may narrow automatically; widening requires an explicit rightful grant"
  privacy: "inherits unless made stricter; never widens by nesting"
  sources: "retain attribution"
  targets: "do not automatically inherit"
  confidence: "does not automatically inherit"
  proof: "rolls up only through a declared parent condition"

structural_change_rule: >
  Create, attach, reparent, merge, and split begin as proposals. Accepted
  changes append an authorized receipt with before and after identities,
  hashes, provenance, preserved disputes, aliases, affected relations, and a
  rollback or compensating path.

invariants:
  - "Topical similarity is not containment."
  - "Spatial proximity is not containment."
  - "same_as requires identity proof stronger than overlap."
  - "Merge never erases source records or disagreement."
  - "Split preserves derived-from lineage and shared evidence."
  - "Every canonical Yawn is reachable from one explicit root or primary parent."

links:
  - spec/holarchy.md
  - core/world-field-arena.yawn
  - core/routing.yawn
  - schemas/agency-holarchy.v0.2.schema.json
